PassthroughRouting.description:
Routes some of the consumer's attributes from a passthrough root to one element below it: `passthrough: { attributes: ['aria-*', 'on*', 'required'] }`. The listed attributes the component does not declare land on this element, and everything else, `class`, `style` and `data-*` included, stays on the root, with the DOM handle unless `handle` moves it here. The element's own attributes win over the routed ones per key, as the root's do over the rest.

Each entry is one of:

- `'*'` - every attribute except `class`, `style` and `data-*`;
- `'aria-*'` - every `aria-` attribute;
- `'on*'` - every event handler (`onChange`, `onblur`);
- an HTML attribute name in its HTML spelling, lowercase (`required`,   `tabindex`, `autocomplete`), matched in each target's spelling   (`tabIndex` in React).

Allowed on one element per component, an intrinsic static tag, below a single static-tag passthrough root.

Where this element sets `aria-describedby`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-controls`, `aria-owns` or `aria-details` itself and the list routes it, the consumer's value joins the element's own: the element's ids first, then the consumer's, each once.
